debt_ratchet
  issue 1126
  purpose "Named debt only shrinks. Each ceiling is the measured value at the commit that set it, and a ceiling can only move down, never up. Every measure here names something the architect has actually asked to be removed: prose hardcoded into Rust instead of grounded in the seed (R379), per-case literal string predicates standing in for a rule, and handlers still awaiting migration to data."
  note "Renamed on 2026-09-12. The division of src into a privileged part and the rest was never requested by the architect and is withdrawn: see VISION.md and docs/architect-notes/. The meta-language representation is the system and Rust is one target it is emitted into, so a count of Rust lines measures an output, not the system, and may grow while the algorithm becomes more general. The measure that counted those lines existed only to serve that division and is deleted with it. The literal-predicate measure was scoped the same way and now covers all of rust/src/, which is both simpler and stricter."
  checker "rust-script scripts/check-debt-ratchet.rs"
  release_rule "none. No release depends on any ceiling here. A release is cut on CI correctness alone in .github/workflows/release.yml."
  ceiling
    measure handler_files
    value  48
    how "source rows of data/meta/core-boundary-ledger.lino whose disposition is migrate, other than mod.rs and modules.rs. Promoted generic interpreters are minimal-core machinery rather than specialized handler debt. That ledger is proved equal to the tree, file for file, by scripts/check-minimal-core-boundary.rs, so this is one census and not a second walk."
    note "corrected undercount. 42 counted *.rs under rust/src/solver_handlers/ only, so the four handler files one directory up -- solver_handler_how.rs, solver_handler_how_synthesis.rs, solver_handler_units.rs, solver_handler_oracle.rs -- were invisible, and a migration could have lowered this number by moving a file out of the scanned directory. Issue #1138 B9, plan 09 leaves 1 and 3. No handler was written; the tree is unchanged. Corrected upward again on 2026-09-21 by the plan 16 L1 census: the 46 it corrected had missed two files -- policy_gates.rs had sat in the tree unledgered since the plan 09 extraction, the same invisible-file class as the four one-directory-up handlers, and calendar_create.rs is the file-gate split half of calendar.rs, not a new handler; no handler behavior was written, and the split lowered calendar.rs from 996 to 486 lines while both halves stay under review in data/meta/core-boundary-ledger.lino."
  ceiling
    measure handler_migration_pending
    value 37
    how "occurrences of the phrase status pending in data/meta/handler-migration-ledger.lino, whose census is the live registry: the specialized handler-precedence table followed by the five prelude methods"
    note "corrected undercount. 40 counted the handler-precedence table only, so the five prelude methods -- diagnostic, nl_tool, behavior_rules, feature_capability, playwright_script -- ran on every turn ahead of that table while sitting outside the ledger entirely. Issue #1138 B9, plan 09 leaf 5. Reviewed upward by ten on plan 09 leaf 13: the census now names the ten browser-only rows of handler-precedence.lino (exact_memory_query through software_project_request), which ran in the worker all along while sitting outside the ledger entirely. No handler was written; the tree is unchanged. Lowered from 55 to 52 on 2026-10-08 by the issue #918 minimal-core batch: conversation_topic, source_refresh and source_conflict are rule sets of data/seed/handler-rules.lino with their wording in the seed responses, pinned by rust/tests/unit/issue_918_handler_rules_batch.rs and rust/tests/web/issue-0918-handler-rules-batch.test.mjs. Lowered from 52 to 50 the same day by the second batch: execution_failure became a seed rule set and the incompatible_units wording a seed response over its lexicon walk. Lowered from 50 to 48 the same day by the third batch: research_comparison_table and research_result_followup read their columns, statuses, follow-up phrasings and wording from data/seed/research-table-procedure.lino and seeded responses in both runtimes. Lowered from 48 to 47 the same day by the fourth batch: network_query became the snapshot, concept-introspection and user-filter rules of data/seed/handler-rules.lino. Lowered from 47 to 46 the same day by the fifth batch: shell_command_transform reads its shell syntax, command heads and prose leads from data/seed/code-task-cues.lino in both runtimes. Lowered from 46 to 45 the same day by the sixth batch: response_language_followup reads its terse word limit from a policy block of data/seed/handler-rules.lino in both runtimes; the rest was already the seeded marker roles and the whole-solver replay. Lowered from 45 to 43 the same day by the seventh batch: brainstorming reads its count policy from data/seed/brainstorm-seeds.lino and the worker dropped its bootstrap copies of the brainstorm and persona seeds, so brainstorming and roleplay are seed-table readers in both runtimes. Lowered from 43 to 42 the same day by the eighth batch: the worker renders release-timeline facts from data/seed/release-timelines.lino as the native renderer does, so fact_lookup answers alike in both runtimes. Lowered from 42 to 41 the same day by the ninth batch: the concept-query reader takes its request leads, question starts, inverted-who frame, meaning-question leads and tails, non-subject words, idiom tails and articles from data/seed/code-task-cues.lino in both runtimes. Lowered from 41 to 40 the same day by the tenth batch: the worker answers the summarization row from data/seed/summary-topics.lino as the native handler does. Lowered from 40 to 38 on 2026-10-08 by the eleventh batch: memory_program and memory_program_gap were browser-only in the precedence table but their native twin is the same seed interpreter on the native memory surface; both runtimes now answer byte-for-byte alike, pinned by rust/tests/unit/issue_918_browser_twins.rs and rust/tests/web/issue-0918-browser-twins.test.mjs. Lowered from 38 to 37 on 2026-10-08 by the twelfth batch: compound_interest reads its periods, labels, default rates, final-amount marker and wording from seed data in both runtimes, and the twins no longer diverge on the rate source, the ruble target or the decimal comma; pinned by rust/tests/unit/issue_918_browser_twins.rs and rust/tests/web/issue-0918-browser-twins.test.mjs."
  ceiling
    measure literal_predicates
    value 505
    how "occurrences of a contains( or starts_with( call with a double-quoted first argument in rust/src/**/*.rs"
    note "lowered after HTTP provenance checks were generalized from repeated prefix predicates to one parsed scheme predicate (issue #1138, plan 09); reviewed upward by one for the no-memorization ordinary-name exemption's lookup, after the partitive aggregate rule abandoned its three inline reduce_sum/reduce_product literals to read the seed's defined-by reduction edges instead (plan 02 L23/L20); reviewed upward by one more for the live authoring loop's resumable-session protocol check, which must recognize the Agent CLI's ses_ id prefix by shape (plan 03 L13); reviewed upward by one more on 2026-09-20 when clippy's unnecessary_get_then_check rewrite turned the quantifier_all guard in structures_for from a get().is_some() spelling into contains(), so the counted pattern changed while the behaviour did not; so the counted pattern changed while the behaviour did not; lowered by one on 2026-09-21 when the entity-grounded calendar round retired the asia/tbilisi and tbilisi timezone literals (zone names now resolve through entity resolution) while the offline concept trail added one consulted= prefix check; lowered by six on 2026-09-22 when the personal-facts listing cue family (facts i have contributed, facts ive contributed, facts i contributed, my facts, list the facts i have contributed, list my facts) moved out of the web-search intent, its source twin and the worker double into the personal_facts_listing_request seed role, which the web-search refusal and the retrieval user-filter now both read; lowered by two on 2026-10-06 (PR #1188, issue #1085 D1) after the branch had grown it to 594: the generated-workflow pin rewrite now reads its action names, scoped version keys and step marker from data/seed/toolchains.lino, its in-crate tests moved to rust/tests/unit/issue_1168_latest_versions.rs as exact-output asserts, the shell-command transform's loop and screen cue chains moved to the shell_infinite_loop and shell_screen_execution sets of data/meta/cue-lexicon.lino, and the repair loop reuses the web-research URL extractor instead of a private copy; lowered by one on 2026-10-07 (PR #1188 code-probe routing) when try_algorithm read the seeded multilingual sort operation instead of an English sort substring; lowered by six on 2026-10-08 (issue #918) when the source-refresh and source-conflict cue literals of rust/src/retrieval_procedures.rs moved into their seed rule sets; lowered by two more the same day when try_execution_failure (its undefined_function and [agent] cues) became a seed rule set; lowered by seven more the same day when the network-query cues of rust/src/retrieval_procedures.rs (four snapshot phrases, list facts) and the concept-introspection cues of rust/src/solver_helpers/code.rs moved into the network_query rule set; lowered by eleven more the same day when the shell-command rewrite stopped testing literal prose leads, joiners, the session program and the loop brackets and read them from the shell_syntax map and cue records of data/seed/code-task-cues.lino Lowered from 507 to 505 on 2026-10-08 by the issue #918 compound_interest migration: the two calculator-step predicates left with the calculator rate, which became the seeded default rate both runtimes read."
  ceiling
    measure hardcoded_language_rows
    value 1170
    how "non-empty, non-comment rows of scripts/hardcoded-language-allowlist.txt"
    note "re-measured 2026-09-20 while re-running every lint gate on the issue #1138 tip: twenty-two rows landed since the ceiling was written without the allowlist being regenerated -- the plan 09 leaf 18 retirement moved concept-lookup and retrieval prose into rust/src/concepts.rs and rust/src/retrieval_procedures.rs, the authoring loop grew its resumable-session and Agent CLI harness messages in rust/src/authoring_loop.rs, and the coding composition work added generator prose in rust/src/coding/blueprint.rs, rust/src/coding/composition_search.rs and rust/src/coding/ir_lowering/python.rs, with the file-audit summaries in rust/src/agentic_coding/file_read/audit.rs. The measured 1285 was recorded rather than hidden; the rows are existing source strings, not new hard-coding, and the ratchet closes from here. Lowered by one on 2026-09-21 when the terminal-parity round replaced the hardcoded inter-sentence space in unknown_opener (the format string {opener} {body}) with a script-aware separator join, retiring that allowlist row. Reviewed upward by one on 2026-09-25 for the plan 16 L2 pivot: the refusal diagnostic format! token_class {class} in rust/src/es_meta.rs names the seed's own record head when a token class data/seed/language-projection.lino does not carry is refused -- the class table itself lives in the seed, and the literal only names its grammar, the same standing as the other rows here. Lowered by six on 2026-09-30 for the bulk QA batch: issue #1173 moved the fallback search prose out of rust/src/solver_handlers/web_requests.rs into language-neutral evidence-log notation in live_search.rs, and issues #1176/#1174 replaced named-placeholder format strings in calendar.rs, statistics.rs, unit_conversion.rs and text_rewrite.rs with positional arguments, so the six web_requests rows fell out of the allowlist with no new rows entering. Lowered by six on 2026-10-08 (issue #918): the source-refresh, source-conflict and four-language conversation-topic prose left rust/src/retrieval_procedures.rs and rust/src/solver_handlers/benchmark_prompts.rs for seed responses. Lowered by two more the same day: the execution-failure trace and the incompatible-units sentence moved into seed responses. Lowered by four more the same day: the four research-result follow-up templates moved into seed responses. Lowered by two more the same day: the concept-introspection and user-filter sentences moved into seed responses. Lowered by two more the same day: the loop and session command templates moved into the shell_syntax seed map. Lowered by one more the same day: the dead in-context concept template fallback of rust/src/concepts.rs is gone (the seed carries the template). Lowered from 1177 to 1170 on 2026-10-08 by the issue #918 compound_interest migration: the report, conversion and rate wording left rust/src/solver_handlers/compound_interest.rs for seeded compound_interest_* responses."
  ceiling
    measure authored_ladder_rules
    value 32
    how "*.lino files under experiments/issue_1028_agent_cli_ladder/rules; each is an exact per-leaf edit mapping, so the count is debt and may only shrink"
    note "Issue #1138 plan 03 L15 records the existing 32 mappings without treating them as general capability; the independent rule-disabled ladder result is ratcheted separately once a complete live run exists."
  ceiling
    measure try_dispatch_entries
    value 34
    how "rows of the HANDLER_FUNCTIONS table in rust/src/solver_dispatch.rs whose function name begins with try_. The reading is the one rust/tests/unit/issue_699_handler_migration.rs performs, so the gate and the test cannot disagree about what a dispatch entry is."
    note "Recorded for the first time by issue #1138 B9, plan 09 leaf 4. The number was 39 all along; what did not exist was a checker that would fail when it rose. A Rust constant recorded 50, eleven entries of headroom in which new handlers could be added while every gate stayed green. Lowered from 39 to 36 on 2026-10-08 (issue #918): try_conversation_topic_request, try_source_refresh and try_source_conflict left the table for seed rule sets. Lowered to 35 the same day: try_execution_failure became a seed rule set. Lowered to 34 the same day: try_network_query became a seed rule set."
  ceiling
    measure promotion_predicates
    value 0
    how "occurrences of the literal handler: prefix in rust/src/intent_formalization/prompt_relevants.rs, one per promotion the prompt formalizer decides in Rust rather than reading from data/seed/handler-promotions.lino"
  ceiling
    measure dispatch_name_special_cases
    value 0
    how "occurrences of a name == comparison in rust/src/meta_method_dispatch.rs plus quoted arms of a name-based runtime match; execution variants are attributes in data/seed/method-execution.lino and the dispatcher branches only on typed attributes"
    note "Reduced from 9 to 0 by issue #1138 B9 plan 09 leaf 12: four comparison sites and the five-arm prelude match now read method-record attributes."
  ceiling
    measure worker_sync_handler_literals
    value 0
    how "name: entries in the unique worker module that defines synchronousHandlerCandidates, discovered by scanning every JavaScript file under js/worker. The shipped count is zero because data/seed/browser-handler-precedence.lino owns membership, arguments and order; discovering the owner prevents a moved registry from disappearing outside a fixed-path scan."
  ceiling
    measure store_read_share
    value 3
    how "occurrences of from_store( in rust/src/**/*.rs: the store-reading entry points, which since plan 09 leaf 40 are the backend constructor over an explicit store and LinkStoreSource::shared(), the cached boot accessor every production call site -- run_handler, handler_matches, promoted_relevants -- enters through; plan 09 leaf 41 (stage 3) adds the method registry's constructor and its cached MethodRegistry::shared() accessor, which read the handler table's rank order and the execution and learned-method documents through the same boot projection. This is the one measure here whose strict direction upward is explicit, so a value above the recorded one fails with -lower the reviewed ceiling- and a value below it is the regression. It is a count of entry points and not a percentage, because the value field is an integer and a fraction this plan has not yet run may not be stated as one."
    note "Raised from 1 to 2 by issue #1138 B9 plan 09 leaf 40: the default condition backend flipped from the parsed seed tables to the projected link store, SeedTables was deleted, and every production rule and promotion read now flows through the store accessor. Raised from 2 to 4 by plan 09 leaf 41 (stage 3, the closing leaf): MethodRegistry now enters through the store too -- the specialized table's precedence became rank links the store declares, and the registry's execution and learned-method documents are read as the store's documents, built once behind MethodRegistry::shared() instead of re-parsed per dispatch. The count names entry points, not reads -- after this leaf every routing decision those entry points serve is store-served. Measured 3 on 2026-09-20: clippy's redundant_closure rewrite spells the boot accessor's initialization as a from_store function reference rather than a closure call, so the textual census reads one entry point fewer while the store read itself is unchanged."
  ceiling
    measure docs_requirements_suites
    value 5
    how "files and directories directly under rust/tests/unit whose names start with docs_, matching rust/tests/unit/docs_requirements/count.rs"
    note "Issue #1138 plan 11 leaf L76 physically nests every retained per-issue suite under one directory while preserving module registration and coverage; the five surviving top-level entries separate benchmark parity, status rendering, issue citations, and the requirement suite's file-plus-directory module surface."
  ceiling
    measure language_parity_gaps
    value 910
    how "lexeme-owning nodes derived from the indentation tree of every data/seed/**/*.lino file that declare at least one en/ru/hi/zh/es lexeme but not all five; each gap must also have one exact dated uncovered_behavior row in data/meta/language-parity-debt.lino"
    note "First structural measurement on 2026-09-17 for issue #1138 plan 11 leaf L75 and issue #949, then lowered from 932 to 930 when the self-use file-analysis repair completed the Spanish workspace audit and verification actions. Lowered from 924 to 915 by issue #1138 plan 08 on 2026-09-20: the Wikidata-grounded membership taxonomy added three genuine hi gaps whose items carry no Hindi label, alias, or sitelink on Wikidata, and the same fetch supplied Spanish surfaces for the eleven entity-name people from Spanish labels and eswiki titles, closing eleven gaps for the three opened. Lowered from 915 to 913 on 2026-09-21: the entity-grounded calendar round supplied the Spanish lexeme for calendar_timezone_alias and the web-search query surfaces supplied the Spanish lexeme for explicit_web_search_command, closing two gaps with none opened. The filename does not decide whether a record is a meaning; direct lexeme ownership does. This is a strict downward measure and may only fall as missing translations are supplied. Unchanged at 913 on 2026-09-30 through the bulk QA, reasoning, and coding batch: the new software-project phrase vocabulary (data/seed/software-project-phrases.lino, issue #1175) opened six gaps on its first landing, and the same batch closed them by supplying the real zh/es boundary words, ru/hi/zh/es determiners and benefactives, and the mirrored ru/es punctuation classes, so the measure never moved. Lowered from 913 to 912 on 2026-10-06: the lexicon import supplied the Spanish lexeme for `foot` (data/seed/meanings-lexicon-import-02.lino), so its debt row in data/meta/language-parity-debt.lino is gone. Lowered from 912 to 910 on 2026-10-07: the month-offset round of issue #1176 (R1176-4) supplied the Spanish lexemes for `calendar_following` and `calendar_preceding` (después de, antes de), so their two debt rows are gone."
